<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Most Loaded Breakfast Item</h2>
<p>The Ultimate Hash Browns Platter takes a base of crispy hash browns and piles on sausage, scrambled eggs, cheese, and country gravy. It is essentially a full savory breakfast built onto a potato base — one dish instead of separate eggs, meat, and sides. At 790 calories it is filling without reaching the ~1,000 calories of the <a href="/categories/breakfast">Country Breakfast Platter</a>.</p>
<h2>Availability Comes First</h2>
<p>Like all DQ breakfast, this platter is served only at select locations, mostly across the South and Midwest, and generally only until around 10:30 AM. Check with your <a href="/locations">local DQ</a> before planning a breakfast run — the majority of stores do not serve it.</p>
<h2>How It Compares</h2>
<p>Against the <a href="/items/buttermilk-pancake-platter">Buttermilk Pancake Platter</a> ($5.49, 680 cal), the Hash Browns Platter is the savory counterpart — choose based on whether you want sweet or savory. If you want something lighter or portable, the Breakfast Burrito or Biscuit &amp; Gravy are smaller and cheaper.</p>
